  <desc>Price levels: how far above cost each kind of customer pays.</desc>
    <credit type="author">
      <name>Reuben Rissler</name>
      <email>pygtk.posting@gmail.com</email>
    </credit>
  </info>

  <title>Customer markup</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Administration</gui><gui>Customer markup</gui></guiseq>
  keeps the price levels, such as retail, contractor or wholesale. Each
  customer is given one in <link xref="contacts#edit">their contact</link>,
  and each product has a selling price for each level on its <link
  xref="product_edit_main#pricing">Pricing</link> tab.</p>

  <list>
    <item><p><gui>New</gui> adds a level; click its <gui>Name</gui> to rename
    it, and its <gui>Markup</gui> for the usual percent above cost, which new
    product prices start from.</p></item>
    <item><p>Check <gui>Default</gui> on the level new contacts start with. The
    default level's prices are also the ones on shelf labels and reports of
    retail price.</p></item>
    <item><p><gui>Delete</gui> deletes the selected level; if customers still
    use it, you are asked which level to move them to, then click
    <gui>Update and Delete</gui>.</p></item>
  </list>

</page>
